    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:p1-normal-inverse .
  ex:p1-n28-v rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:p1-log-tasks .
  ex:p1-n41-v rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:p1-variance-compare .
  ex:p1-n46-v rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:dist-t-compare .
  ex:p1-n63-v rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:p1-pearson-contributions .
  ex:rv-f-v rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:dist-f .
  ex:rv-log-v rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:p1-log-transform .
  ex:rv-n14 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-normal ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:normal-measurement-model ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:nn-cdf-f ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:nn-cdf-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-normal-v ;
    cd:narration "N14. Move one threshold and follow the density coordinate and CDF ordinate together. At 10.20 mg/L, standardized distance two gives left probability 0.977249868 and upper probability 0.022750132. Phi is an antiderivative of the standard-normal density. No elementary antiderivative exists; express it with the special error function erf after scaling the argument and applying the half-offset. erf itself is not a probability. The integral from minus infinity fixes the CDF normalization. A density height is not a probability. The finite drawing does not truncate the mathematical law."@en .
  ex:rv-n15 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-normal ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:normal-measurement-model ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:nn-tail-f ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:nn-tail-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:p1-n15-v ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-normal-r ;
    cd:narration "N15. Ask for the upper exceedance probability before moving the threshold. The stable method can exceed 10.20 by chance in about 2.275 percent of individual results. This is neither a fault diagnosis nor a regulatory specification. Keep inverse mode off for this forward calculation."@en .
  ex:rv-n16 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-normal ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:normal-measurement-model ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:nn-ecdf-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n16-r ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n16-v ;
    cd:narration "N16. These are the same seeded individual draws as N08, not a new fitted dataset. Change the prefix length and compare empirical steps with the full fixed model CDF. At 1,000 readings and 10.20 mg/L the empirical fraction is 0.978. Finite-sample agreement cannot prove normality."@en .
  ex:rv-n16-r rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:CodeRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:optionalCode "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:hasCodeExample" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:nn-ecdf-code .
  ex:rv-n16-v rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:p1-ecdf-start .
  ex:rv-n17 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-normal ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:normal-measurement-model ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:nn-decision-f ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:nn-decision-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:p1-n17-v ;
    cd:narration "N17. Ask the inverse question: choose a one-percent upper rate. The required threshold is 10.232634787 mg/L. This per-result known-parameter calculation is not automatically calibrated for repeated monitoring or estimated model parameters."@en .
  ex:rv-n22 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-lognormal ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:lognormal-concentration-model ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:lg-saved-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:lg-saved-v ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n22-r ;
    cd:narration "N22. Compare fictional repeat injections with separately constructed full-preparation outcomes. Their histogram shapes motivate questions about absolute and relative influences; they do not establish a population distribution from a small sample. Keep the independent preparation design visible and preserve the raw data in the extended path."@en .
  ex:rv-n22-r rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:CodeRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:optionalCode "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:hasCodeExample" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:lg-compare-code .
  ex:rv-n25 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-lognormal ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:lognormal-concentration-model ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:lg-definition-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-log-v ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n25-f ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n25-r ;
    cd:narration "N25. A normal dimensionless log ratio becomes a positive skewed concentration after exponentiation. Increase log SD while holding median fixed. The arithmetic expectation rises; symmetry is on the log scale, not on the concentration axis. The simulated process is an assumed model, not empirical validation."@en .
  ex:rv-n25-f rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:lg-definition .
  ex:rv-n25-r rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:CodeRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:optionalCode "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:position "4"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:hasCodeExample" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:lg-transform-code .
  ex:rv-n28 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-lognormal ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:lognormal-concentration-model ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:lg-tail-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:p1-n28-v ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n28-f ;
    cd:narration "N28. First read the forward question at 15 ng/L, then the inverse question at a five-percent upper rate. Both panels are visible together. At log SD 0.30 the forward upper probability is about 0.08826 and the inverse threshold about 16.38 ng/L. Retain concentration units after back-transformation."@en .
  ex:rv-n28-f rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:lg-quantile .
  ex:rv-n29 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-lognormal ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:lognormal-concentration-model ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:lg-checks-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n29-c ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n29-r ;
    cd:narration "N29. Changing the sampling unit changes the population. Across-site environmental variation is not repeatability of one homogeneous preparation. Mixtures, reporting limits and censoring can distort both raw and log-scale shape. Preserve arithmetic and geometric reporting distinctions without asserting normality from positive values."@en .
  ex:rv-n29-c rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:DefinitionListRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:hasDefinitionListEntry" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:p1-population-cards .
  ex:rv-n29-r rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:CodeRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:optionalCode "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:hasCodeExample" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:lg-environment-code .
  ex:rv-n31 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-chi ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:al-chi-square ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:ic-question-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n31-v ;
    cd:narration "N31. Announce a new fictional six-reading nitrate QC series. Repeatability, not bias, is the question. Compare with a fixed SD reference of 0.10 mg/L under normal independent readings. The CRM series will be another clearly announced study. Treat the validation SD as known for this teaching comparison; if its estimation uncertainty matters, use a different justified variance comparison. Prespecify a one-sided increased-spread alternative at five percent."@en .
  ex:rv-n31-v rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:ic-process-media .
  ex:rv-n32 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-chi ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:al-chi-square ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:ic-deviations-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:ic-deviations-t ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n32-f ;
    cd:narration "N32. Center the six QC readings at their own sample mean 10.05 mg/L, not the nominal ten. The residual sum of squares is 0.12 (mg/L) squared. Divide by five to get variance 0.024, then take the positive root to get sample SD about 0.155 mg/L. Distinguish units at every step."@en .
  ex:rv-n32-f rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:ic-spread .
  ex:rv-n34 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-chi ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:al-chi-square ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:ic-repeated-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-variance-r ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-variance-v ;
    cd:narration "N34. Hold six readings per complete series and true SD fixed. Change simulation count or seed. A sample variance is random even under an unchanged stable method. The observed QC variance is separately marked as 0.024. The next construction explains the distribution instead of treating the histogram as a proof."@en .
  ex:rv-n36 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-chi ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:al-chi-square ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:ix-sum-f ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:ix-sum-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n36-v ;
    cd:narration "N36. Change independent components from one to two to five. Squared standard-normal terms add their degrees of freedom. Independence matters; six centered residuals share an estimated mean and cannot simply be treated as six such independent terms."@en .
  ex:rv-n36-v rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:p1-five-squares .
  ex:rv-n41 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-chi ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:al-chi-square ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:ix-size-f ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:ix-size-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:p1-n41-v ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-variance-r ;
    cd:narration "N41. Compare six and thirty readings per series directly on the same variance grid while holding true precision fixed. Relative SD of the variance estimate falls from 63.2 to 26.3 percent. More Monte Carlo series only improve the picture. Larger Q means can reflect larger df, not poorer precision. A second uncertain variance motivates F; first consider a mean with an uncertain denominator."@en .
  ex:rv-n44 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-t ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:l5-student-t ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n44-c ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-student-v ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:tf-denominator-h ;
    cd:narration "N44. Repeat whole independent normal series. Each mean is divided by its own estimated SE. Small denominator estimates create heavier tails without changing the underlying individual-reading model. Start with n two, giving one Student degree of freedom, and inspect both density overlays before moving to the derivation."@en .
  ex:rv-n44-c rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:DefinitionListRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:hasDefinitionListEntry" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:tf-denominator .
  ex:rv-n46 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-t ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:l5-student-t ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:p1-n46-v ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n46-c ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:tf-df-live-h ;
    cd:narration "N46. Compare Student densities with three and twenty-nine degrees of freedom and the standard normal limit. Increasing the number of independent normal readings stabilizes the estimated denominator. Discuss shape, symmetry and tail weight, without introducing a test or an observed CRM case."@en .
  ex:rv-n46-c rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:rv-n46-info .
  ex:rv-n46-info rdf:type cd:Interpretation ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body """- **More measurements:** a more stable estimated denominator.
- **More degrees of freedom:** lighter tails, closer to the normal density.
- **Same center:** the distributions remain symmetric around zero."""@en ;
    cd:bodyFormat "markdown" .
  ex:rv-n49 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-f ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:l5-f-distribution ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:dist-devices-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n49-f ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n49-v ;
    cd:narration "N49. Two fictional independent groups illustrate two sample variances. Preserve all six readings in each group. A has mean 10.10 and SD 0.10, B mean 10.00 and SD 0.30 mg/L. The descriptive B/A variance ratio is nine; do not make a population decision from it. The following simulation explains the ratio's distribution."@en .
  ex:rv-n49-f rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:tf-ratio .
  ex:rv-n49-v rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:rx-devices .
  ex:rv-n50 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-f ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:l5-f-distribution ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-f-v ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:tf-f-live-h ;
    cd:narration "N50. Equal true variances do not force equal sample estimates. Simulate independent pairs and inspect the random B/A ratio. A small denominator creates a long right tail. Equal means are not required for the variance-ratio reference. Do not infer the true ratio from the observed nine."@en .
  ex:rv-n60 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-tests ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:rev-qq ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rev-qq-read-c ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rev-qq-read-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rev-qq-read-v ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n60-f ;
    cd:narration "N60. New constructed five-reading A and B samples, not devices A and B from the variance study. Plot observed ordered readings against quantiles of a fixed normal model with mean ten and SD 0.50 mg/L. A follows the identity line; B bends. A freely fitted line would instead emphasize shape. Five points cannot establish normality."@en .
  ex:rv-n60-f rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "4"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:rev-qq-formula .
  ex:rv-n61 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-tests ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:l5-kolmogorov-smirnov ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rev-ks-overlay-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n61-c ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n61-r ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n61-v ;
    cd:narration "N61. Retain the same two samples and fixed normal CDF. KS is the maximum vertical gap, checking both sides of every empirical jump. At n five the exact two-sided 5% cutoff is 0.563275. A distance 0.144578 does not reject, B distance 0.725747 rejects. Estimated parameters require a different calibration, not the fixed-CDF table. The extended path retains the symbolic supremum definition and its complete legend."@en .
  ex:rv-n61-c rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:DefinitionListRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:hasDefinitionListEntry" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:rv-n61-info .
  ex:rv-n61-decision rdf:type cd:DefinitionListEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "Fixed model: compare both distances with 0.563275"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "Normal mean 10 and SD 0.50 mg/L are fixed before sampling. Five independent continuously distributed measurement results give the exact two-sided 5% cutoff 0.563275. A: distance 0.144578, do not reject. B: distance 0.725747, reject. Non-rejection does not prove normality. Compare vertical gaps at both sides of every ECDF jump."@en ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:rv-n61-fitted rdf:type cd:DefinitionListEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "A model fitted to these data needs another reference"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "If mean and SD are estimated from these measurement results, the fixed-model cutoff is no longer calibrated. Use a suitable Lilliefors calibration or parametric bootstrap refitting every replicate. Standardizing the observation axis is optional; probabilities do not change. Ties, censoring and dependence also require matching calibration."@en ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:rv-n61-info rdf:type cd:DefinitionList ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:rv-n61-decision ;
    cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:rv-n61-fitted .
  ex:rv-n61-r rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:CodeRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:optionalCode "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:position "5"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:hasCodeExample" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:rev-ks-code .
  ex:rv-n61-v rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:rev-ks-media .
  ex:rv-n62 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-tests ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:l5-pearson-gof ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rev-pearson-start-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n62-f ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-pearson-v ;
    cd:narration "N62. New grouped particle-count study, independent of the Q-Q and KS readings. One hundred classifications use five fixed exhaustive categories and probabilities. Expected counts ten, twenty, forty, twenty, ten; observed four, twelve, forty-four, twenty-four, sixteen. Contributions 3.6, 3.2, 0.4, 0.8, 3.6 sum to 11.6. This categorical approximation is not the exact sample-variance law."@en .
  ex:rv-n62-f rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:l5-p20a-formula .
  ex:rv-n63 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-tests ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:l5-pearson-gof ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:p1-n63-v ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rev-pearson-table-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n63-r ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:v3-n63-f ;
    cd:narration "N63. Calculate the first contribution: four minus ten, squared and divided by ten gives 3.6. Add all five weighted discrepancies to get 11.6. No fitted category probabilities, so the fixed total leaves four df. Compare with cutoff 9.487729, p 0.020587. Compatible counts give 0.225 without changing the rule. Non-rejection cannot establish the model and rejection does not identify the cause."@en .
  ex:rv-n63-r rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:CodeRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:optionalCode "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:position "4"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:hasCodeExample" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:rev-pearson-code .
  ex:rv-normal-r rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:CodeRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:optionalCode "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:position "4"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:hasCodeExample" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:nn-threshold-code .
  ex:rv-normal-v rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
