<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/scenes/level5-review-opening> {
  ex:rv-n02 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-functions ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:l5-analytical-distributions ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n02-c ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n02-h ;
    cd:narration "N02. The title is N01 and is supplied by the presentation renderer. Announce the entire route, including the transformed-normal lognormal branch, model checks and uncertainty propagation. This is a multi-session package. Ask how the random quantity changes from readings to estimates and decisions; do not promise that the whole package fits one ninety-minute meeting."@en .
  ex:rv-n02-c rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:DefinitionListRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:hasDefinitionListEntry" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:p1-route .
  ex:rv-n02-h rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:rv-n02-title .
}

<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/scenes/level5-review-p1-scenes> {
  ex:p1-n12 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-z ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:normal-measurement-model ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:nn-eta-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:p1-n12-v ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:v3-n12-f ;
    cd:narration "N12. Uppercase Z is the standardized random variable; lowercase z is one observed standardized value. The marked result 10.20 mg/L has z two under known mean ten and SD 0.10. z is dimensionless, not a probability. Leave the probability question open for the CDF and upper-tail scenes. Standardizing a nonnormal variable does not make it normal."@en .
  ex:p1-n12-v rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:v3-normal-coordinate .
  ex:p1-n13 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-z ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:normal-measurement-model ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:nn-devices-f ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:nn-devices-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:p1-n13-v ;
    cd:narration "N13. Compare two assumed known-parameter device models on one concentration axis before reading the calculation. The same 10.20 mg/L is two SDs from the narrower expectation and one from the wider. These known SDs 0.10 and 0.20 are not the estimated SDs from the later device comparison."@en .
  ex:p1-n13-v rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:p1-normal-devices .
  ex:p1-n18 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-normal ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:normal-measurement-model ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:nn-bands-f ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:nn-bands-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:p1-n18-v ;
    cd:narration "N18. Compare a one-percent upper event with two symmetric tails outside one, two or three SD. Compute central coverage from the accumulated probabilities rather than learning the 68-95-99.7 values as unrelated rules. This concerns individual readings, not confidence intervals for a population mean."@en .
  ex:p1-n18-v rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:p1-normal-bands .
  ex:p1-n33 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-chi ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:al-chi-square ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:ix-series-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:p1-n33-v ;
    cd:narration "N33. Plot all six results from each of the same three illustrative series. Their constructed means coincide, but spreads differ. In genuinely repeated sampling, means would generally vary too. The next slide places these three estimated variances in a distribution of complete-series variance estimates."@en .
  ex:p1-n33-v rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:p1-series-chart .
}

<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/scenes/level5-review-pdf-cdf> {
  ex:pc-n03 dct:references ex:cf-readings ;
    dct:subject ex:l5-topic-functions ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:cumulative-distribution-function ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:pc-n03-c ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:pc-n03-h ;
    cd:narration "Start with three analytical questions: how often in an interval, how much below a limit, and which limit gives a chosen probability? Introduce nitrate repeatability through the instrument process, then distinguish a finite simulated histogram from a population PDF and CDF. The named distribution families come later. The twenty-reading dotplot, empirical threshold warm-up and adjustable-bin scene are retained as optional extended material, not required here."@en .
  ex:pc-n03-c rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:DefinitionListRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:hasDefinitionListEntry" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:pc-questions .
  ex:pc-n03-h rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:pc-questions-title .
  ex:pc-n07 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-functions ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:normal-measurement-model ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:pc-n07-c ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n07-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n07-v ;
    cd:narration "N07. Keep the nitrate repeatability question, without introducing another six-reading dataset. Point to small disturbances along the instrument process. They can motivate an additive model, but do not establish independence or normality. The next histogram is a stated simulation model, not newly collected evidence."@en .
  ex:pc-n07-c rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:pc-process-info .
  ex:pc-n08 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-functions ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:probability-density-function ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:pc-n08-c ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n08-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n08-r ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n08-v ;
    cd:narration "N08. Grow the same seeded simulation prefix from twenty to fifty, one hundred and one thousand results under fixed model parameters. Normality is an assumption of this generator, not a conclusion from the original twenty measurements. More simulations show the assumed shape more clearly, not better physical precision. Next distinguish an empirical histogram from the model's theoretical density; no combinatorial detour is needed."@en .
  ex:pc-n08-c rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:pc-growth-info .
  ex:pc-n09 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-functions ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:probability-density-function ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:pc-n09-f ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:pc-n09-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:pc-n09-v ;
    cd:narration "These thousand results are explicitly simulated under an assumed model, not laboratory measurements. Overlay the population density on its finite histogram. Narrow the chosen interval without confusing density height with probability. A histogram estimates a density; it does not become an exact PDF just by drawing thinner bins. The same tools also apply to the bounded flat alternative. Neither the optional twenty-reading warm-up nor a binomial construction is required."@en .
  ex:pc-n09-f rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:pc-area .
  ex:pc-n09-h rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:pc-density-title .
  ex:pc-n09-v rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:pc-density .
  ex:pc-n10 dct:references ex:pc-n09 ;
    dct:references ex:theoretical-quantile ;
    dct:subject ex:l5-topic-functions ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:cumulative-distribution-function ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:pc-n10-f ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:pc-n10-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:pc-n10-v ;
    cd:narration "N10. Move one shared threshold and watch left density area become the CDF ordinate. Ask where the CDF is steepest, then connect its local slope to the PDF wherever the derivative exists. Reverse the question: choose cumulative probability 0.95 and read the quantile. The generalized inverse is not a reciprocal. Show the bounded flat model briefly to establish that these tools are not specific to the Normal family. Only next identify phi and Phi as standard-normal special cases."@en .
  ex:pc-n10-f rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:pc-functions .
  ex:pc-n10-h rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:pc-linked-title .
  ex:pc-n10-v rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:pc-linked .
  ex:pc-n11 dct:references ex:pc-n10 ;
    dct:subject ex:l5-topic-normal ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:normal-measurement-model ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:nn-phi-f ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:nn-phi-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:pc-n11-v ;
    cd:narration "N11. The class already knows general f and F. Now identify the standard-normal PDF as one particular f, written lowercase phi. Many sufficiently small additive influences can motivate an approximate normal law when appropriate central-limit conditions hold; dominant, dependent or heavy-tailed effects require care. A combinatorial binomial derivation is optional extended material, not a prerequisite. Phi lowercase is density, not a point probability. The next scenes define the standardized coordinate and specialize F to uppercase Phi."@en .
  ex:pc-n11-v rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:pc-phi-chart .
}

